From 5dd5bd59dfee872210b6738692ecbde34c3c37d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:18:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(logging): configurable errors/gateway/gui log rotation;
 INFO trace for dropped process completions [daveey]

errors.log (2 MB x 2) and gateway.log (5 MB x 3) rotation was hard-coded, so the busy
hub kept about an hour of history and incidents older than that could not be
root-caused. logging.<stem>_max_size_mb / logging.<stem>_backup_count (stem errors,
gateway, gui) now size them; unset keeps the old sizes. agent.log already follows
logging.max_size_mb / backup_count.

A process completion dropped by the notification park (retention expiry, displaced
by a result), by the unowned-event path (park refused, shutdown drain), or by the
registry's parked-event box overflow was logged at DEBUG or not at all, so a chat
that never woke for a re-adopted exit left no trace. Each now writes one INFO line
"Dropped completion notification for process <proc id> (session=<key>): <why>";
progress notices (watch_*, heartbeat) stay DEBUG.

Tests: tests/tui_gateway/test_notification_park_drop_log.py (4) and two rotation
tests in tests/test_hermes_logging.py; all 5 new behavioural tests fail without the
source change.
